review_comments:
Throwing an error if `this` is used inside the function would be easy, but I'm not completely sure where in the compilation pipeline would be best to throw the error (e.g. whether to do it directly in `reflectObjectLiteral` or somewhere further down the line). 

I'd have to play around with it, but maybe we can do it with types? TS allows for `this` to be typed in functions so we could do something like the following which will flag any accesses of `this`:


```
interface InjectableOptions {
    providedIn: string;
    useFactory?: (this: never) => any;
}

const service: InjectableOptions = {
    providedIn: 'root',
    useFactory() {
        return this.providedIn; // Compilation error
    }
};
```
